== J.7 randomized LP rounding
OK   Pr[edge uncovered] = (1-a)(1-b) <= 1/4, maximized (not minimized) at a = b = 1/2; its minimum is 0
OK   C5, one round: E[w] = LP = 5/2, E[#covered edges] = 15/4 = 3/4 of 5
OK   one round: E[w(x')] = LP exactly; at least 3/4 of the edges covered in expectation
OK   N rounds: Pr[v in C] = 1-(1-x)^N <= N x, so E[w(C)] <= N LP, not = (C5, N=2: 15/4 < 5)
OK   4^(-N) = n^(-4) for N = 2 lg n
OK   K_4, x* = 1/2, N = 4: Pr[C is a vertex cover] >= 1 - 1/n^2  [0.97846985]
OK   K_8, x* = 1/2, N = 6: Pr[C is a vertex cover] >= 1 - 1/n^2  [0.99357900]
