== J.12 an FPTAS for subset sum
OK   exact SubsetSum (sets of sums) = brute force; |S_i| <= min(2^i, t+1)
OK   ApproxSubsetSum: r* <= s* <= (1+eps) r*, so r* >= (1-eps) s*  [worst r*/s* 0.8478]
OK   inductive claim with delta = eps/(2n): every s in S_i has r in R_i with r <= s <= r (1+delta)^i
OK   |R_i| <= |R_{i-1}| + floor(log_{1+delta} i) + 1
OK   the note's ceil(log_{1+delta} i) undercounts at i = 1 (R_1 = {0, x_1})
OK   survivors p of R_{i-1}+x_i: largest/smallest > (1+delta)^(p-1), both in [x_i, i x_i], so p <= floor(L)+1
OK   the note's ceil(log_{1+delta} i) is a valid count for i >= 2 (wrong only at i = 1)
OK   one survivor per interval alone allows floor(L)+2: delta = 1, i = 3, x_i = 3, [3, 9] meets 3 intervals
OK   note's case (2) middle step fails (delta=1/10, i=2, x=5, r=20, r'=17); the corrected chain holds
OK   (1+eps/2n)^n <= e^(eps/2) <= 1+eps for 0 < eps <= 1
OK   ln(1+delta) >= delta/2 on [0,1], so log_{1+delta} n <= 2 ln n/delta = 4 n ln n/eps (not n ln n/eps)
